# THE REGISTER WINDOW: a function with more locals than the window holds one
# register apiece (MAXREG 200). Ring has no such limit; Ring++ refused the
# function until its locals SHARED registers (shareFunction, 2026-10-18).
# Each section is a shape sharing could get wrong: a value carried past many
# others into a late loop; locals in the two arms of an if; a read of a
# shared register before its own local was assigned (R24, as on Ring);
# try/catch; lists, whose release a shared register must not lose or repeat;
# a local a lambda names. Generated by a script; every line was checked
# against the oracle first.

? Big(3)
? "done"

